    11	   `MEMORY.md` index is readable. Drift signal: breadcrumb + event.
    12	3. **Audit-log flush** — touch the audit-log filelock to ensure
    13	   any pending writes are drained before process exit (best-effort;
    14	   filelock guarantees append order within the session).
    15	4. **Audit-tokens auto-run** — invoke `audit-tokens.py` subprocess
    16	   with 1s wall-clock timeout (PLAN-059 SEC-P0-04 / ADR-080). Default
    17	   ON since Session 67 / ADR-090 #6. Emits `audit_tokens_emitted`
    18	   event when subprocess completes; `audit_tokens_timeout` when it
    19	   exceeds the cap.
    20	5. **Memory-delta observation** (PLAN-179 W2 US8, SPEC v2.60 —
    21	   implements `PLAN-179/staged-w24/SESSIONEND-NOTE.md`). The historical
    22	   question here was "COULD this session have written memory?" (the
    23	   writability bit of #2). US8 adds the one that matters: "DID it?" —
    24	   answered STAT-ONLY (`st_mtime` vs the session-start anchor), one
    25	   `session_memory_delta_observed` event + one operator line. The hook
    26	   NEVER writes memory and never opens a memory file for write: memory
    27	   writing stays a decision of the model or the Owner — this rail makes
    28	   the OMISSION visible, nothing more.
    29	
    30	## Fail-open contract (ADR-005)
    31	
    32	Any internal exception → `{"continue": true}` lifecycle output.
    33	SessionEnd does not ever block the session end — the hook is
    34	observational.
    35	
    36	## Kill-switches
    37	
    38	- `CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0` — disables the entire hook (no-op
    39	  return). Highest priority.
    40	- `CEO_AUDIT_TOKENS_AUTO=0` — disables responsibility #4 only.
    41	  Responsibilities #1-#3 still run. Default is ON (per ADR-090 #6
    42	  Session 67 default flip).
    43	- `CEO_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA` — three-state switch for responsibility
    44	  #5: unset/default = "full" (emit event + operator line);
    45	  `quiet`/`1q` = event only, no systemMessage line; `0`/`false`/`off`/
    46	  `no` = fully off (nothing emitted). Default-ON rationale
    47	  (SESSIONEND-NOTE.md §3): this rail IS the visibility PLAN-179 W2
    48	  depends on — an opt-in rail nobody enables reproduces the very
    49	  omission it measures. The `off` state needs NO gate-side waiver
    50	  (rail r14, corrects the NOTE §104-108 model): the registered command
    51	  stays a real hook (`python3 .claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py`), which the
    52	  harness-config constant-emitter heuristic can never flag — a
    53	  substring allowlist entry would be inert for that purpose while
    54	  creating an ADR-158 §2 bypass for a replaced constant-emitter
    55	  command carrying the same substring.
    56	"""
