   190	
   300	    At SessionEnd any tool that stamped a PreToolUse record but never produced
   301	    a Post/Failure is, by definition, an orphan (the session is ending; it will
   302	    never complete) — so sweep with ``timeout_s=0.0`` to emit
   303	    ``tool_call_lifecycle_recorded`` with ``orphan=True`` for every survivor
   304	    BEFORE evicting the file. This is the production trigger that makes orphan
   305	    detection reachable (MF-PERF-3); without it the affirmative orphan branch
   306	    was dead in production (perf-review must-fix). The sweep emit is the
   307	    deny-by-default scrub-branch action, fail-OPEN.
   308	
   309	    Then ``cleanup_session`` bounds the record-file lifecycle to a single
   310	    session (MF-PERF-2). Best-effort + fail-open: SessionEnd is observational
   311	    and MUST NOT block on this.
   312	    """
   313	    try:
   314	        from _lib import tool_lifecycle  # type: ignore
   315	        # Flush any in-flight (unpaired) Pre records as orphans first.
   316	        tool_lifecycle.sweep_orphans(session_id, timeout_s=0.0)
   317	        tool_lifecycle.cleanup_session(session_id)
   318	    except Exception:
   319	        return
