     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""PostToolUse Agent audit log — Python single-file hook with rotation.
     3	
     4	Port of `.claude/scripts/audit-log.sh` to stdlib Python. Bash version
     5	remains untouched until A.4 flips settings.json to the Python shim.
     6	
     7	## Schema
     8	
     9	Identical to AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md with these additions:
    10	
    11	- `hook_duration_ms` (integer) — wallclock duration of the hook itself,
    12	  measured at end of processing. Enables `audit-query.py stats --latency`
    13	  analysis in Sprint 3 without re-instrumenting the hooks.
    14	
    15	PLAN-020 Phase 0 item 1 (audit-log v2.7 schema bump — ADDITIVE):
    16	
    17	- `usage_metadata` (object|null) — Anthropic API usage_metadata
    18	  passthrough. Keys: `cache_creation_input_tokens`,
    19	  `cache_read_input_tokens`, `uncached_input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,
    20	  `thinking_tokens`. Each is integer or null. Captured per spawn for
    21	  cache-coverage analysis (PLAN-020 §6 sub-target measurement).
    22	- `cache_coverage_bps` (int|null) — derived metric in integer
    23	  basis-points (ratio × 10000, clamped [0, 10000]):
    24	  `cache_read / (cache_read + cache_creation + uncached)`. Null if
    25	  totals unavailable. PLAN-020 §6 acceptance: P50 +10pp vs Phase 0
    26	  baseline. PLAN-118 WS-E (S181): replaced the legacy `cache_coverage`
    27	  float — floats break the HMAC-covered payload (canonical_json
    28	  no-float invariant). The derivation helper still returns the float
    29	  ratio; the producer converts to bps before the entry dict.
    30	- `rail` (string|null) — spawn dispatch rail: `"native"` |
    31	  `"custom"` | null (legacy / unknown). Discriminator for ADR-050
    32	  dual-rail A/B harness. PLAN-019 emitters (pre-PLAN-020) emit null;
    33	  PLAN-020 Phase 1+ emitters set the value.
    34	
    35	All three fields are ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore them safely.
    36	
    37	PLAN-021 ADR-052 (audit-log v2.8 schema bump — ADDITIVE):
    38	
    39	- `model` (string|null) — Claude model ID used for the spawn. Values
    40	  are canonical Anthropic IDs of the CURRENT fleet (e.g.
    41	  `"claude-fable-5"`, `"claude-opus-5"`, `"claude-sonnet-5"`,
    42	  `"claude-haiku-4-5"`; N-1 ids like `"claude-opus-4-8"` remain valid
    43	  in replay), or null if unknown. Captured from `tool_response.model`
    44	  when Anthropic API
    45	  emits it, else null. Enables forensic correlation: if a
    46	  Sonnet-routed review misses a bug, the audit log proves which
    47	  model made the decision.
    48	
    49	Field is ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore; pre-v2.8 emitters emit
    50	null.
    51	
    52	PLAN-065 Phase 1 (audit-log v2.15 — extract_skill 3-path matrix):
    53	
    54	- `extract_skill()` ports the validated 3-path logic from
    55	  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` (58 tests, ReDoS-hardened) inline
    56	  into the hook so audit-log emit covers Format-A inline / Format-B
    57	  reference / Format-C `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Restores
    58	  observability of `skill=<name>` post-ADR-082 mitigated dispatch +
    59	  Format-B SKILL REFERENCE default flip. Pre-Phase 1 baseline: 24/24
    60	  agent_spawn rows had `skill="unknown"` (100% loss). Target ≤10%
    61	  unknown in 30d post-merge.
    62	
    63	  Sec MF-7 hardening: NFKC normalize, NUL byte denied, length cap
    64	  256 chars on captured group, path traversal denied (the captured
    65	  group grammar excludes `/` `..` `\\`), regex bounded quantifiers
    66	  `{0,255}` (no nested unbounded alternation — ReDoS-safe).
    67	
    68	PLAN-079 (extract_skill Path D — canonical archetype mapping):
    69	
    70	- Path D added to `extract_skill()` as a TAIL fallback (after Paths
    71	  A/B/C miss). Maps the 5 canonical archetypes — `code-reviewer`,
    72	  `security-engineer`, `qa-architect`, `performance-engineer`,
    73	  `devops` — to their canonical skill names per ADR-051 (sub-agents
    74	  load skills via `.claude/agents/<name>.md` reference, not inline).
    75	  Closes the observability gap S87/S88 surfaced (20/26 unknown
    76	  agent_spawn rows on canonical-archetype dispatches without
    77	  inline SKILL CONTENT).
    78	
    79	  Backwards compat: signature changed from `extract_skill(prompt)`
    80	  to `extract_skill(prompt, subagent_type="")` — default arg
    81	  preserves all single-arg callers. Frozen mapping constant
