    35	(``scratchpad_lib.open_session_scratchpad``) and reports the new outcome
    36	``written_session_scope``. Per emenda r1-C1 the session id comes ONLY from the
    37	hook input — if the derivation would fall back to ``CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`` (env,
    38	agent-spoofable — consensus M2) the fallback is REFUSED and the outcome stays
    39	``scratchpad_unavailable``; the scope is recorded in the blob's own
    40	``scope_kind`` field, never by overloading ``plan_id`` (the store's
    41	plan-isolation invariant stays intact).
    42	
    43	## Contract
    44	
    45	- ADVISORY + fail-open (PLAN-091 S116 doctrine: parse errors / missing files /
    46	  derivation failures / timeouts → stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{}``). NEVER
    47	  blocks — a crashed snapshot must not stop a compaction.
    48	- Time budget ``TIME_BUDGET_S`` (subprocess git capped; budget-blown → snapshot
    49	  what we have, never noise).
    50	- Emits ONE closed-enum ``compaction_continuity_snapshot`` audit event
    51	  (registered in BOTH ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` and SPEC v2.43) carrying ONLY closed
    52	  enums + counters: ``trigger`` (manual/auto/other), ``snapshot_outcome``
    53	  (written/written_session_scope/scratchpad_unavailable/error/other),
    54	  ``plan_id`` (PLAN-NNN or ``unknown``), ``chain_length`` (clamped int). The
    55	  snapshot BODY (plan path text, checkbox label, ceremony paths, last-hmac
    56	  hex) is written to the scratchpad — NEVER to the audit wire.
    57	- Snapshot privacy: the write is plan- or session-scoped and secrets-redacted
    58	  by ``state_store.set``; the audit emit carries no path/label text.
    59	  **PLAN-179 amendment 8.3 (debate C9):** this claim used to be FALSE on the
    60	  path actually taken — ``state_store.set`` redacts ``isinstance(value, str)``
    61	  ONLY and this hook handed it ``payload.encode("utf-8")``, i.e. bytes, which
    62	  the store trusts verbatim. The snapshot is now passed as a ``str`` so the
    63	  store's own redactor runs. Same rule for the session-scoped write.
    64	- Kill-switch: ``CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`` (shared with the PostCompact
    65	  reinjection half). It also disables the session-store GC below — the switch
    66	  turns the whole feature off, housekeeping included.
    67	- PLAN-179 rail finding C: this hook is the PRODUCTION CALLER of
    68	  ``scratchpad_lib.gc_orphan_session_stores`` (see ``_gc_session_stores``).
    69	  The session-scope fallback creates one sqlite store per unresolved-plan
    70	  session and row-TTL expiry cannot unlink a FILE, so without a caller the
    71	  fallback accumulated files without bound. The sweep runs last, is bounded by
    72	  the library's own per-run cap, respects the remaining time budget and is
    73	  fail-open: no snapshot outcome depends on it.
    74	- PLAN-179 W0 US2b progress guard: OBSERVE + NOTIFY only (see
    75	  ``_progress_guard``); it emits ``context_pressure_observed`` and a stderr
    76	  breadcrumb, and is DISABLED unless ``CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS`` is
    77	  set. It cannot halt a compaction — PreCompact has no deny channel.
    78	- Stdlib only, Python >= 3.9.
    79	
    80	## Scratchpad key
    81	
    82	``compaction_continuity`` (single JSON blob, <64 KiB; ``set`` overwrites). The
    83	PostCompact half reads this exact key — in the plan scope first, then (PLAN-179
    84	W1 US3) in the session scope.
    85	"""
    86	from __future__ import annotations
    87	
