SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:499:| `context_pressure_observed` (v2.56) | `action`, `used_bucket` (int — CLOSED set of PERCENT rungs: `40` / `60` / `80` / `90` / `95`; the unit lives in the field NAME. The check `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected (it is an `int` subclass, so `True` would otherwise sail through any numeric test) and `float` is rejected even when it COMPARES equal to a rung (`40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python), because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event, leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — the same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`. Anything off-set is COERCED to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a coerced one), `event_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `precompact` / `sessionstart_compact` / `userpromptsubmit` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed. Only `precompact` has a shipped producer in the PLAN-179 W0/W1 bundle; `sessionstart_compact` — the channel PLAN-179 debate amendment 8.1 designates PRIMARY — and `userpromptsubmit` are RESERVED, and a consumer MUST read their absence as “no producer yet”, NEVER as “no pressure observed on that channel”. The PostCompact `additionalContext` channel stays UNPROVEN until the PLAN-179 W0-1 probe lands and is therefore deliberately ABSENT from the enum), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`), `session_id` (present ONLY when the producer holds a session id derived from the HOOK INPUT; deliberately OMITTED otherwise rather than filled from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, which an agent can set — an unattributed row is honest, a wrongly-attributed one is not; PLAN-179 amendment r1-C1), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W0 US2 / debate amendment 8.1 (ADR-153 continuity successor rail, 2026-08-18) — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:505:| `session_memory_delta_observed` (v2.60) | `action`, `session_id` (str — threaded from the harness event, clamped ≤128, no silent default), `project` (str — `str(repo_root)`, clamped ≤256, the same field every event on this rail already carries), `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum `written` · `absent` · `index_only` · `start_unknown` · `dir_missing` · `not_writable` · `error` · `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, NEVER to `written` — an unparseable observation must never be laundered into a healthy-class value), `files_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries in the native memory dir), `modified_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries whose `st_mtime` falls inside THIS session's window — a WINDOW-scoped observation over the SHARED per-project dir: a CONCURRENT session's write inside the window counts (ADR-005 overlap is a supported case) and stat carries no author, so this is never an authorship claim), `index_modified` (bool — `MEMORY.md` specifically; non-bool coerced to `false`), `anchor_source` (str — CLOSED enum `chain` · `state_file` · `none`: which step of the session-start resolution answered — the HMAC chain's own `session_start` event via bounded scan (≤200 lines / ≤256 KiB / ≤100 ms; the OLDEST in-window match wins — a compact-restart re-emit for the same session id must not shrink the window — and a candidate is consumed only after its per-entry HMAC verifies against the previous line with the project key (verify-before-consume, ADR-160; `CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE=1` waives the integrity claim; scope is PER-ENTRY — the candidate against the ADJACENT line's declared digest, the predecessor itself NOT re-verified: a same-UID log writer reads the 0600 key and forges whole chains anyway (CLAUDE.md §5 boundary), so whole-chain integrity stays `verify_chain`'s offline job, never this bounded reader's claim); the chain is the anchor, never a mutable side file — the ADR-160 §3 / A6 principle), `state_file` — RETIRED in this same ceremony (rail r5: the record file is rewritten via `os.replace` on every tool update, which allocates a NEW inode and resets even `st_birthtime` — no immutable artifact exists on that surface); the enum value stays registered for wire-compat and is NEVER produced. Resolution is therefore chain-or-`none`, with REAL predecessor resolution on the chain leg (legacy `hmac:null` prefix lines are traversed to the last SIGNED line, mirroring `verify_chain`; genesis applies only when the bounded window covers the whole file), or the terminal `none` = "I do not know": the hook never substitutes "since midnight" or process start, because a wrong window produces a false `written`, worse than absent), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US8 (wave-179-close ceremony; implements the signed spec `PLAN-179/staged-w24/SESSIONEND-NOTE.md`) — SessionEnd memory-delta observation: ONE emit per session from `.claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py::decide`, immediately BEFORE the `session_end` emit so a reader scanning backwards from `session_end` finds it adjacent. STAT-ONLY producer: counts `st_mtime >= session_start` over the native memory dir and NEVER opens a memory file for write — memory writing stays a model/Owner decision; the count is window activity over the project dir, not per-session authorship (rail r6 P2-a); this action makes the OMISSION visible (`outcome=absent` is the case the historical `memory_writable` bit could not express; structural namespace activity — rename/delete, detected via the directory mtime inside the window — BLOCKS the absence class and the index_only exclusivity, because the closed enum cannot express a structural delta and `error` is the honest refusal — rail r17). A NEW action deliberately, not extra fields on `session_end`: overloading would conflate "the hook ran" with "a delta was observed" and change the meaning of an event with a landed row (v2.7). Typed producer `emit_session_memory_delta_observed` routes through the dedicated deny-by-default `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion + TYPE-strict int clamps (bool is an int subclass, and a float would drop the ENTIRE event at the canonical-json layer — both coerce to the sentinel 0, never rounded, never echoed), NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire, by name — the scrub operates on field NAMES (non-allowlisted keys are dropped; identity fields `session_id`/`project` are type-checked and clamped, their VALUES being the emitter-wide baseline contract every action shares — the typed wrapper is the sole sanctioned producer and `test_no_paths_on_the_wire` pins what it sends): the memory file names/basenames (rail r22: names travel on NO channel at all — five rail rounds of directive-smuggling bypasses proved free-form basenames unsanitizable for an instruction-adjacent surface, so the operator line is COUNTS-ONLY and the sanitized `names` list remains an internal gate for any future render; this supersedes the earlier "names to the operator" split of the W2 AC, deviation declared), the file bodies or any excerpt, the resolved memory-dir absolute path and the `$HOME`-derived slug, the raw `session_start` source line, any environment value. Kill-switch `CEO_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA` (unset = full; `quiet`/`1q` = event only, no operator line; `0`/`false`/`off`/`no` = nothing emitted — the `off` state needs NO gate-side waiver (rail r14, correcting the SESSIONEND-NOTE §104-108 model): the registered command remains a real hook, which the harness-config constant-emitter heuristic can never flag, and a substring allowlist entry would be inert for that purpose while opening an ADR-158 §2 bypass). Completeness residual (honest boundary, same as ADR-153 §H2): an ABSENT row is not evidence of an absent session — `CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0`, `disableAllHooks`, or a killed process all suppress it. Pre-registered DEATH criterion (SESSIONEND-NOTE.md §8): `outcome=absent` dominating a measurement window with no behaviour change means the rail is REMOVED, not kept as debt. NO ATLAS technique (governance/omission-visibility breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:530:| `compaction_continuity_snapshot` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `trigger` (str — CLOSED enum: `manual` / `auto` / `other`; coerced to `other`), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape, else `unknown`), `chain_length` (int — clamped 0..99999999), `snapshot_outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `written` / `written_session_scope` / `scratchpad_unavailable` / `error` / `other`; coerced to `other`; `written_session_scope` added v2.56 / PLAN-179 W1 US3 — the snapshot WAS written, but to the SESSION-scoped fallback location because `resolve_plan_id()` could not name a plan. That is the S309 fires-proof DOMINANT path, not an edge: a `plan_transition` is emitted only on a status CHANGE, so a long session — exactly the kind that compacts — normally carries none of its own (S309 census: 2 events in 12,515 audit lines). Kept DISTINCT from `written` so a ledger can separate plan-scoped from session-scoped continuity instead of conflating the two; the enum stays CLOSED and anything else still coerces to `other`), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H1 (anthropic-surface-harvest; ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PreCompact governance snapshot: before the harness compacts a long session (manual `/compact` or auto context-window threshold), `check_precompact_continuity.py` snapshotted plan-id + execution-unit position + pending-ceremony flags to the plan-scoped scratchpad + read the audit HMAC-chain anchor (last-hmac prefix + chain-length). ONE emit per compaction event. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_precompact_continuity.py` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — `settings_tamper_detected` precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY_SNAPSHOT_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the snapshot BODY — the plan path text, the execution-unit checkbox label, the ceremony script paths, the full last-hmac hex (the snapshot lives in the plan-scoped, secrets-redacted scratchpad; the wire carries closed enums + the chain_length counter only). Honest coverage boundary: ADR-153 §H2 (a hook is disarmed by `disableAllHooks`; S3 boot tripwires + W5 O10 OTEL witness are the named compensators). NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:531:| `compaction_context_reinjected` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape, else `unknown`), `snapshot_found` (bool — coerced to `false`), `snapshot_age_s` (int — clamped 0..9999999), `pointer_count` (int — clamped 0..9; POINTERS ONLY. Its meaning is UNCHANGED by PLAN-179, deliberately: a counter that is silently re-scoped makes its own historical series uncomparable, so the constraint block below got a NEW counter instead of a widened one. A consumer may compare `pointer_count` across the whole v2.43+ series), `constraint_count` (int — v2.56 / PLAN-179 W1-b, amendment r1-C3: the count of PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINTS re-stated verbatim after compaction, sourced from `_lib/pinned_constraints.constraint_count()` — the SET size, never the rendered LINE count, because the block carries a header line and a counter that drifts with formatting is not a counter. Constraints and pointers hold SEPARATE budgets: the 9-line pointer cap can never truncate a governance rule. Treatment in the scrub branch: `max(0, min(99, int(...)))` with the same `except (TypeError, ValueError) -> 0` fallback the sibling counters use. **STATUS — both halves land in THIS ceremony (PLAN-179 W0/W1):** `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch carries the clamp above, so the deny-by-default scrub KEEPS the field and `check_postcompact_reinject.py` puts a real clamped `int` on the wire. A consumer MUST still read an ABSENT `constraint_count` as “this producer predates constraint pinning”, NEVER as “zero constraints pinned” — absence and zero are different facts, and `constraint_count=0` is itself meaningful (it is what `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0` produces)), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H1 (anthropic-surface-harvest; ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PostCompact governance reinjection: after compaction, `check_postcompact_reinject.py` read the PreCompact snapshot from the plan scratchpad and reinjected governance POINTERS (active PLAN, execution-unit position, Gate-1 re-read reminder, pending ceremonies, HMAC anchor) via `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. POINTERS ONLY — never file CONTENTS (the Option-A prompt-injection surface, ADR-153 §Decision). ONE emit per PostCompact event. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the reinjected pointer TEXT, the plan path/label, the ceremony paths, the scratchpad body (only the closed enums + counters persist). PLAN-179 W1-b [r1-C3] prepends a PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT block AHEAD of the pointers: a pointer is not a restriction — ADR-153's pointers say WHERE the rules live, the pinned block re-states the rules THEMSELVES from a CODE constant (`_lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS`), never from disk, so the prompt-injection reasoning that forces POINTERS-ONLY on the snapshot simply does not apply to it. The constraint TEXT is no more on the wire than the pointer text — only `constraint_count` is. Dedicated kill-switch `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0`, deliberately SEPARATE from `CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`: an operator disarming the continuity SNAPSHOT must not silently disarm the governance floor. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
