SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:587:| v2.56 | PLAN-179 W0 US2 + W1 US3 + W1-b (context-continuity successor rail / ADR-153, debate amendments 8.1 + r1-C3, 2026-08-18) — 1 NEW metadata-only action `context_pressure_observed` (EDGE-TRIGGERED: emitted only on a percent-rung TRANSITION, gated by `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(...)` against the `context-pressure-last-bucket` marker under the gitignored `.claude/state/` — per-session when the producer supplies a session id (`<basename>.<sanitized-id>`), falling back to the bare project-wide basename otherwise, a documented degraded mode in which two concurrent sessions in one repo can interfere with each other's hysteresis; hysteresis, never sampling — a per-turn sampler would append one row per prompt while the session sits in one rung), PLUS 1 additive value on the EXISTING closed `snapshot_outcome` enum of `compaction_continuity_snapshot` — `written_session_scope`, the S309 fires-proof DOMINANT path where the snapshot lands in the session-scoped fallback because `resolve_plan_id()` could not name a plan — PLUS 1 NEW bounded field `constraint_count` on the EXISTING `compaction_context_reinjected` action. NO new typed emitter: `context_pressure_observed` goes through `emit_generic` (compaction-pair / `settings_tamper_detected` precedent) into a dedicated deny-by-default `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`; `plan_id` reuses the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator. **`used_bucket`'s integer typing is normative, not stylistic:** `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict (rejects `bool`, an `int` subclass, and rejects `float` — `40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python, so a plain membership test would wave a float onto the wire and `_lib/canonical_json.py` would then drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb; same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`). Off-set values coerce to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the `{40,60,80,90,95}` enum. **`pointer_count` is UNCHANGED** and keeps counting POINTERS ONLY — constraint pinning landed as the SEPARATE `constraint_count` rather than by re-defining what `pointer_count` measures, because a silently re-scoped counter makes its historical series uncomparable (amendment r1-C3 is what makes this SPEC bump non-optional). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. Registered via the PLAN-179 W0/W1 pack ceremony (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 324 -> 325; the staged set literal measures 325). **CODE/ROW PARITY — three integration gaps were found by the W0/W1 cross-file pass and are CLOSED by this same ceremony, so this row describes the wire as shipped, not as intended:** (1) `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch clamps it `max(0, min(99, int(...)))`, so the deny-by-default scrub keeps it; (2) the shipped producer of `context_pressure_observed` (`check_precompact_continuity.py:_progress_guard`) probes `getattr(audit_emit, "should_emit_context_pressure", None)` — the name that actually exists — and calls it with the crossed bucket, `state_dir = <project>/.claude/state` and the trusted session id, retrying the two-argument shape on `TypeError` so an adopter whose `audit_emit` predates per-session markers degrades to the project-wide marker instead of losing the observation; an earlier draft probed `edge_trigger_should_emit`, a name in neither library, which suppressed every emit; (3) that producer now sends the allowlisted trio `used_bucket` / `event_source` / `plan_id`, where `used_bucket` is the PERCENT rung from `_context_used_pct` + `_pressure_bucket` and the rung SET is DERIVED from `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` at call time rather than restated ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]); the earlier `used_tokens_bucket` (`used_tokens // 10000`) and `floor_tokens` are gone from the wire and survive only in the operator's stderr breadcrumb, which is the correct home for a raw count. A conformance test asserting this row against the wire is expected to pass. **Producer coverage is still partial and that is not a defect of this row:** `precompact` is the only `event_source` with a shipped producer; `sessionstart_compact` and `userpromptsubmit` remain RESERVED, and their absence means “no producer yet”, never “no pressure observed on that channel”. | *(1 additive value on the existing `_COMPACTION_SNAPSHOT_OUTCOMES` closed enum; 1 additive field on `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`; 1 new per-action allowlist `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` + closed sets `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT` / `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCES` + type-strict validator `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` + edge-trigger helper `should_emit_context_pressure` and marker basename `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_STATE_BASENAME` in `audit_emit.py`; new module `_lib/pinned_constraints.py`)* |
