   631	       pre-PLAN-179 adopter, any exception out of the sweep: breadcrumb and
   632	       return. The snapshot above it has already been written and its outcome
   633	       is already on the wire — housekeeping may not retro-actively change it.
   634	    2. **Cheap and bounded.** PreCompact fires at most once per compaction, so
   635	       no extra throttle is invented here (a timestamp file would be a second
   636	       piece of state to get wrong). The work is one directory listing plus at
   637	       most ``MAX_GC_FILES_PER_RUN`` unlinks — the cap is the LIBRARY's, not
   638	       a number recalled here
   639	       ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]). The remaining
   640	       budget is honoured: a run that already blew ``TIME_BUDGET_S`` skips the
   641	       sweep rather than adding to the overrun.
   642	    3. **TTL matched to what this hook WRITES.** ``ttl_seconds`` is passed
   643	       explicitly as :data:`SESSION_SNAPSHOT_TTL_S` (7 days) because the
   644	       library default is 72h, and a 72h mtime cutoff would unlink a store
   645	       whose rows this hook wrote with a 7-day TTL — deleting a snapshot that
